<article class="env-definition" id="02ZB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02ZB">Definition <span data-tag="02ZB">8.2.2</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category. Let $p : \mathcal{S} \to \mathcal{C}$ be a fibred category, see Categories, Section <a href="/tag/02XJ" data-tag="02XJ">4.33</a>. Given an object $U$ of $\mathcal{C}$ and objects $x$, $y$ of the fibre category, the <em>presheaf of morphisms from $x$ to $y$</em> is the presheaf </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (f : V \to U) \longmapsto \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _{\mathcal{S}_ V}(f^*x, f^*y)  \]
</div>
  <p> described above. It is denoted $\mathit{Mor}(x, y)$. The subpresheaf $\mathit{Isom}(x, y)$ whose value over $V$ is the set of isomorphisms $f^*x \to f^*y$ in the fibre category $\mathcal{S}_ V$ is called the <em>presheaf of isomorphisms from $x$ to $y$</em>. </p>
</article>